  "details": "VRChat used to have a 'red' age verified profile badge, but was removed because \"Red looked really bad on some headsets and didn't match our visual design.\"\n\nDespite this, if some tweaks could be made to the icon, I feel like it could be repurposed for the better of improved instance discovery.\n\nWhen creating an instance that requires 18+ verification, there should be an option for the host to either choose \"General age verified instance\" (featuring the standard blue age gated icon), or \"Contains sensitive content\" (with a red, or different color badge) as a caution sign for users before they enter.",
